How to make a ren release

1. Put the entries for the release in NEWS under a header like
   "* Noteworthy changes in release 1.2.0 (unreleased)".

2. Set the version in configure.ac (AC_INIT).  Use the next minor number
   for a new feature and the next patch number for fixes only.

3. For a release that adds or changes translatable messages, send a release
   candidate to the Translation Project first:

     git tag -a v1.2.0-rc1 -m "ren 1.2.0-rc1" && git push origin v1.2.0-rc1

   The workflow publishes a pre-release whose tarball unpacks to
   ren-1.2.0-rc1.  Email its URL to the coordinator, wait about a week,
   then fetch the new .po files and commit them.

4. Put the release date in the NEWS header, commit, and tag:

     git tag -a v1.2.0 -m "ren 1.2.0" && git push origin master v1.2.0

   The workflow (.gitea/workflows/release.yml) builds, runs make distcheck,
   and publishes the tarball and SHA256SUMS as a Gitea release.  It fails
   if the tag and the configure.ac version differ, or NEWS has no section
   for the release.

To check the build without publishing, run the "release" workflow by hand
from the Actions page.
